label("5",(3/2,9/8),NE);
draw(((0,-7/8)--(0,-9/8)));
label("3",(-3/2,-7/8),S);
label("3",(3/2,-7/8),S);
[/asy] By the Pythagorean theorem, the altitude shown is $\sqrt{5^2-3^2}=4$.

Now we can draw and label a radius of the circle: [asy]
unitsize(20);
